-- title:
--   Obstruction 2-cochain as a pinned point derivation at the unit
-- statement:
--   Let $T'$ be an Artinian local ring with residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,T'$, let $\pi\colon T'\to T$ be a ring homomorphism whose kernel $I=\ker\pi$ satisfies $I\cdot\mathfrak m_{T'}=0$ and $I\subseteq\mathfrak m_{T'}$, and let $f_0\colon A_0\to\operatorname{Spec}T$ be separated. Let $V$ be a finite $k$-vector space, also a $T'$-module compatibly (with the central right action), and $\iota\colon V\to T'$ an injective $T'$-linear map whose image is $I$. Let $\mathcal U$ be an ordered affine cover of $A_0$ (a finite linearly ordered index set, affine opens $U_a$ with $\bigsqcup$-supremum $\top$), with smooth $q_a\colon Y_a\to\operatorname{Spec}T'$ and morphisms $g_a\colon U_a\to Y_a$. Let $f_k\colon A_k\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ carry a relative group law $L_k$, let $i_0\colon A_k\to A_0$ be an affine morphism, let $U_e\subseteq A_k$ be an affine open and $e_1\colon\operatorname{Spec}k\to U_e$ a lift of the unit section $L_k.\mathrm{one}$. Assume given opens $O_a(W)\subseteq Y_a$, affine whenever $W\subseteq U_a$ is affine, ring isomorphisms $\sigma_s\colon k\otimes_{T'}\Gamma(Y_{s_0},O_{s_0}(\mathcal U_s))\cong\Gamma(A_k,(i_0^{-1}\mathcal U)_s)$ for every strictly increasing $s$ (where $\mathcal U_s=\bigcap_j U_{s_j}$ and $i_0^{-1}\mathcal U$ is the preimage cover) satisfying $\sigma_s(x\otimes 1)=x$, and, for each triple $r=(r_0<r_1<r_2)$, isomorphisms $\rho^{ab}_r,\rho^{bc}_r,\rho^{ac}_r$ between the open subschemes $O_{r_i}(\mathcal U_r)$; writing $u_r$ and $v_r$ for the two resulting morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}\Gamma(Y_{r_0},O_{r_0}(\mathcal U_r))\to Y_{r_2}$ obtained from $\rho^{ac}_r$ and from $\rho^{ab}_r$ followed by $\rho^{bc}_r$ (via the canonical isomorphism with the spectrum of the sections), assume both lie over $\operatorname{Spec}T'$, i.e. composing with $q_{r_2}$ gives $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map, and that they agree after pullback along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient by the ideal generated by $I$. Assume finally that for each $c$ the square formed by $(i_0|_{U_c})$ followed by $g_c$, the inclusion of $i_0^{-1}U_c$ followed by $f_k$, $q_c$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map is a pullback. Then there is a $k$-linear map $\omega\colon\Gamma(A_k,U_e)\to\operatorname{Hom}_k(V^\vee,\check C^2(i_0^{-1}\mathcal U;\mathcal O))$, where the target is the $2$-cochain module $\prod_s\Gamma(A_k,(i_0^{-1}\mathcal U)_s)$ of the unit $\mathcal O$-module presheaf, satisfying the Leibniz rule $\omega(ab)=\mathrm{ev}(a)\omega(b)+\mathrm{ev}(b)\omega(a)$ for the evaluation $\mathrm{ev}$ at $e_1$, such that for every triple $r$ there is a family $cs\colon\Gamma(A_k,U_e)\to\operatorname{Hom}_k(V^\vee,k\otimes_{T'}\Gamma(Y_{r_0},O_{r_0}(\mathcal U_r)))$ which is a system of tangent coordinates for the pair $(u_r,v_r)$ in the sense of `IsTangentCoordsOfPairAtVia` — there are morphisms $w_0$ from the spectrum of the thickening `thickening T' V C`, $C=\Gamma(Y_{r_0},O_{r_0}(\mathcal U_r))$, to $i_0^{-1}U_{r_2}$ lying over the relative tangent base, and $w_1$ to $U_e$, with the predicate `IsTangentOfPair I V ι C` holding for $u_r$, $v_r$ and $w_0$ followed by $(i_0|_{U_{r_2}})\!\gg\! g_{r_2}$, with $w_1$ followed by the inclusion of $U_e$ equal to the $L_k$-translate of $w_0$, and $cs=\mathrm{tangentCoords}$ of the chart homomorphism of $w_1$ — and such that $\sigma_r(cs(a)(\xi))=\omega(a)(\xi)_r$ for all $a\in\Gamma(A_k,U_e)$ and $\xi\in V^\vee$.
--
--   This produces, out of a system of smooth local lifts of $A_0$ along a small extension $T'\to T$ together with triple-overlap comparison isomorphisms, a single point derivation at the unit of the special fibre whose values on each triple overlap are the canonical tangent coordinates of the two competing morphisms; it is the construction step feeding [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_pointDerivations_obstruction_two_cocycle_of_local_lifts`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_pointDerivations_obstruction_two_cocycle_of_local_lifts), where the resulting $2$-cochain is shown to be a cocycle and becomes the obstruction class to lifting the group law.
